<p>When applying booklet-printing to documents containing a mixture of 
 landscape and portrait pages, you can specify whether to print document 
 pages whose orientation differs from the paper orientation rotated by 
 90 degrees or reduced in size without being rotated.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="orientation" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Printout Result:</span></p>
<p>Specify a printout result when you apply booklet-printing to documents 
 containing a mixture of landscape and portrait pages.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Rotate to a Naturally Readable Direction</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">When you apply booklet-printing to documents containing 
 a mixture of landscape and portrait pages, document pages whose orientation 
 differs from the paper orientation are not changed, but rotated to a naturally 
 readable direction.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Reduce without Rotation</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">When you apply booklet-printing to documents containing 
 a mixture of landscape and portrait pages, document pages whose orientation 
 differs from the paper orientation are not rotated, but reduced so they 
 can be printed in the same direction.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this dialog box to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
